        "type": "header",
        "content": "Customization charges"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "Checkout only charges money that exists as real cart line items. Use the store product handle customization-charge priced at $20.00 (recommended) with a single Default Title variant. One customized product → quantity 1 ($20); two → quantity 2 ($40). A $1.00 product still works but checkout will show a high quantity (e.g. 20)."
      },
      {
        "type": "product",
        "id": "customization_fee_product",
        "label": "Customization fee product",
        "info": "Optional if handle customization-charge exists. Prefer $20.00 + Default Title variant so checkout shows title only with quantity 1 per customized product."
      },
      {
        "type": "header",
        "content": "File upload → Dropbox"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "Dropbox access tokens must stay on a server. From the repo root run npm run dropbox-upload (or node dropbox-upload/dropbox-upload-proxy-server.mjs), deploy it publicly, then paste that URL below. With sync enabled and no per-field upload endpoint, the storefront posts files to the proxy and they land in the Dropbox folder. If a field uses Cloudinary (or similar), the proxy also supports Dropbox save_url after that public URL is returned."
      },
      {
        "type": "checkbox",
        "id": "dropbox_sync_enabled",
        "label": "Enable Dropbox upload / sync",
        "default": false
      },
